Structure after the MicroDuck simulator by Pollen Robotics
(https://huggingface.co/spaces/pollen-robotics/microduck-simulator, Apache-2.0).
No code or assets from it are included.

Runs on MuJoCo (Apache-2.0, Google DeepMind) through the @mujoco/mujoco
WebAssembly bindings, three.js (MIT), React (MIT) and zustand (MIT), installed
by npm and not included here.

The robot's 3D model is NOT included and is NOT covered by the licences above.
tools/fetch_sdk_model.py copies it from the Vector Python SDK
(anki_vector/opengl/assets). It is licensed by Anki, Inc. under the Anki Image
and 3D Model License Agreement, version 1.1; the copy carries that licence
text beside it. The part grouping and pivots used to pose it are taken from
anki_vector/opengl/opengl_vector.py (Apache-2.0).

Local demo replacement parts by Dauler (CC NonCommercial as marked in each
original archive). "Anki Vector Wheels v2" https://www.thingiverse.com/thing:3764077
and "Anki Vector Lifting Forks" https://www.thingiverse.com/thing:3731746.
tools/fetch_print_parts.py fetches the originals from Internet Archive. These
STLs are distributed separately from this repository's code and are placed
in public/robot/sdk/print with the original attribution and licence wording.

The optional WireOS body/camera/cube adapter interoperates with the
wire-os-victor simulator protocols at commit 3cec4844d24c4719b5b3892e4979494bcd260424
(https://github.com/os-vector/wire-os-victor). Upstream firmware and headers
are obtained separately; the C++ interoperability test includes those headers.
Its cube mark PNGs under src/game/cube-marks/wireos/ carry the GNU GPL v3.0
notice in src/game/cube-marks/wireos/LICENSE.

The optional detailed animation rig (`tools/fetch_rig_model.py`, slicing
`Victor_rig_01.obj`), charger dock meshes (`tools/fetch_dock_model.py`, fetching
`Vic_charger_hp_geo.obj`), and Light Cube rig (`tools/fetch_cube_model.py`,
normalizing `Victor_cube_rig.obj`) come from kercre123/vector-animations-raw
and follow the Digital Dream Labs Software Asset License v1.0 (`DDL-ASSET-LICENSE.txt`).

The optional standalone real-firmware runtime (`tools/fetch_firmware.py`)
downloads unmodified `cube.dfu` (Dialog DA14580 Light Cube application) and
`syscon.dfu` + `sysboot.bin` (STM32F030 body syscon image) at build/setup time
from os-vector/wire-os-victor at commit 3cec4844d24c4719b5b3892e4979494bcd260424
(Apache-2.0) without storing firmware binaries or keys in git. In-browser
execution uses `src/sim/thumb.js` + `src/sim/cube_firmware.js` (ARMv6-M Thumb VM)
and `src/sim/syscon_firmware.js` (CRC-32 spine framing).
